hello everyone in a few weeks from now a  new badge of students is going to enter  their first year here at iit kharagpur  similarly across various institutes of  india  students have already either joined or  are about to join  various engineering streams as well as  science streams so i thought this would  be a good time for me to share some of  my experiences  give some pointers dispel certain  misconceptions that students invariably  have at this stage i know i did back  when i was a student uh  about to enter my first year here at iit  kharagpur and i wished at that stage  somebody would sit down with me and help  to clear some of my doubts now that i  have gained certain experiences as an  engineering student first myself and  then as a faculty member over the past  few years  i think i'm in a good position to share  some of my experiences and i think some  of you will find it useful and actually  i got the idea of making this video  after seeing the wonderful response of  so many students  to the video that i had made as a  reaction to the  speaks  so if you look at the comment section so  there are a number of students about to  join their first year who have written  to me uh so i think they'll definitely  find it useful all right so number one  point on the academic side  so  the number one misconception which  students invariably have is that they  are going to join first year and then  they are going to start learning  subjects this is not going to happen  okay in the semester system you do not  learn subjects  you learn courses there's a difference  between the two  so what you do in courses  well in a course what you do is to  actually study the sub the the sequence  the exact sequence of topics which your  professor have  which your professors have selected for  you they've already done this job by  scrutinizing the various books and  selecting and extracting  only the parts which are immediately  relevant for you which are important for  your professional career as well as to  prepare you for your higher studies  so trust them and follow the course  material which have been prepared by  them  this does not mean that you should not  try to learn the subject but that will  come a little bit later  very relevant to this point is that many  students think that they are going to  learn a course by starting from a book  this is absolutely wrong  okay please do not try to study from  books on your own  rather the trick is that  from the sequence of topics which your  professor has  given to you and from the way that he or  she is teaching to you  you first try to learn what he's  teaching what he or she is teaching and  then  only after you have gone through those  parts you go back to your book and try  to study the relevant parts from that  that is the way to study otherwise  you see in a semester system you barely  have 100 days or so  and i am also including the saturdays  and sundays here  so in these 100 days  it is simply not possible to study from  books i'll show you something  this semester i'm teaching mechanics of  solvency because this is not a first  year subject this is a second year  subject but things are more or less the  same  let me show you the books okay  so this is one book  this is another book  and this is another book  and now you cannot see my face  so  you really think you can go through all  these books because we we give maybe one  or two textbooks and then give others as  reference materials you simply cannot go  through all of them it is humanly not  possible  so study only the relevant parts from  the books  next  grades  so  don't let anyone mislead you into  thinking that grades are not important i  know in engineering colleges especially  some of the seniors have this habit of  telling their juniors that grades are  not that important it is completely  wrong do not believe them  okay higher grade is always better  however i will also say that  do not fall into the rat race of  just mindlessly mindlessly chasing  higher grades  okay  that is kind of unhealthy  try to maintain a respectable grade  point average  and  you must also understand that  in reality  some things may always go sideways okay  they'll invariably go sideways in a  particular semester  so if as a result your grade point  average decreases a little bit  it does not mean the end of the world  okay please do not think like that  so this directly ties into the next  advice that i'll give to you is that  be a little bit pragmatic in your  approach  okay what i mean by that is that suppose  in a certain semester or in a certain  subject certain things have gone  sideways sideways means something bad  has happened okay maybe one test or  assignment has gone bad this does not  mean that you just give up i have seen  many many students do this okay  something goes wrong and then they just  give up  this is just foolish  what you need to do if something does go  wrong is to just pick up the pieces and  try to do damage control except the fact  that something has gone wrong okay be an  adult about it  except that something has gone wrong and  try to fix it try to do some damage  control okay if you just give up  it will go from bad to worse and that  bad thing in one subject is start is  going to start affecting your other  subjects and then everything will go bad  in that semester okay and you will  become extremely sad so it's a disaster  don't let that happen do some damage  control  all right  next point is regarding projects so  uh i have seen that many first-year  students they have their like bundle of  energy and they  uh  they try to start doing some projects  some academic projects try to approach  some professors this is not the right  approach  this is not the right approach because  when you have not even completed your  first year you barely know the subjects  okay so the way that we follow in most  of the iits in all the ideas rather is  that the first year curriculum is common  okay you only get to start learning the  departmental subjects properly in the  second year so unless you have gone to  the second year studied the third  semester courses  up to that point you are not well  prepared to take up a proper academic  project so little so have a little  patience until that time comes okay at  the the first year is not the right time  for you to take up a project  okay  there's a special tip for iitns here  you see all of you  and this is common knowledge but i think  i'll be  i'll be remiss if i don't say this  all of you have been kind of academic  stars of your particular batches maybe  it is in school in college  in your coaching center whatever  you have been kind of academic stars  this is going to end once you enter  the iit's  you are no longer going to be the stars  because it's it's a common sense thing  right so all the academic stars have  joined together so everyone is a star  you are nothing special  okay i know it can be kind of i mean sad  to think about it but this is the truth  it's a great privilege that you get to  have as your peers so  uh  so gifted students or capable students  so don't take it as a negative rather  take it as a positive but i assure you  this after all we are all human flesh  and blood  you will feel sad a little bit okay that  you are no longer that that you no  longer have that special status  which you had earlier in school  okay but please try  to not  to let not that affect you  next is regarding various societies or  student groups  uh  i've seen that many students  they  mindlessly chase  after this  after various after after this goal of  joining various societies or student  groups this is not correct  okay it is absolutely necessary for you  to do some activity  in your engineering or science which is  not fetching you marks it is important  to do such kind of activity but at the  same time  if you try to join this you're trying to  join that also you're trying to learn  that also you are going to spread  yourself too thin  you have only a finite amount of time in  your hand  finite amount of energy also  so you should not be spreading yourself  too thin such that the  work that you are doing both in your  curricular activities as well as your as  well as in your co-curricular activities  okay  they get affected in quality  so more than the quantity and the  variety of things that you do try to be  really really good excellent in whatever  little you do that will carry far more  weight  okay  another important thing is that you  should not be shy to ask for help  now i when i was in my first year i was  extremely introverted  okay  i'm still introverted i've just learned  how to fake it a little bit now so  there's that but  uh you absolutely need to ask for help  when you need help  okay so  uh next point is on the social side and  this is very very important okay please  don't close the video just because i've  stopped talking about the academic and  the student group side of things this is  important  on the social side okay  you have to start making friends  i mean seriously good friends  now  uh when i say like this  please don't think of it like some kind  of a business arrangement okay that is  not going to work of course  at the same time  you will never be able to have good  friends  if you're not proactive about it you  have to seek out  friends  and let me tell you this  uh  it is good to have the kind of friends  who you  you like to hang out with but at the  same time you also need to have friends  from whom you can learn something  okay it is not only just the professors  from whom you are going to learn rather  you are also going to learn a lot i mean  in fact a lot of lot of the things from  your peers from your seniors  so try to make some very good friends  there's a very special point i would  like to mention here is that  when you are making these kinds of  friends  try to  make  friends from different kinds of circles  okay so that your mind and your  development  by connection with those friends is not  just one-dimensional okay maybe have  some friends who are good in sports  maybe have some friends who are good on  the cultural side of things maybe they  know how about music about uh about  various cultural things maybe they're  good in writing or or reading  maybe you could pick up some things from  them maybe some someone is very good in  electronics kind of things or in  programming  even if you don't engage in those  activities yourself you will definitely  learn some things from them  that's a valuable thing  okay so everything need not come into  your cv okay there are certain soft  things which you need to pick up also  uh  another thing is that  uh  you also need to have some very very  special friends okay special friends  means like  more than best friend i would say  let me give you a small example here  from my own life when i was an  undergraduate student once  i mean  i just fell ill  okay and fell in like it was like a  sudden illness i mean once i i got up in  the morning and then i just couldn't  raise my head from the bed  so what i did was i just called up my  friend who was in another hostel  actually because mind you this was  winter  there was practically no one in my own  hostel  and so i just called up this friend who  was in another hostel some distance away  this was very very early in the morning  in a winter  i just call him  please come without a single question  asked he got up and came in that morning  he didn't even ask what happened what do  you need nothing he just  heard me saying that please come he just  came  that's it and then he took me to the  hospital help me out so that's that okay  so you need to have that kind of special  friends who can answer to your phone  call at 4 am without any questions asked  all right  so uh  i'm almost at the end of my uh  of this little  advice piece  uh  finally i would like to just point out  one very important thing so i've started  our discussions from point number one uh  but  since um  both thermodynamics and the python  programming language are important to  engineering and science  as a mark of respect to both  thermodynamics and python i will put  this as number zero  and that is your health  none of the things that i have mentioned  earlier  is going to be of any use or any  applicability to you  if you do not maintain your health  okay i am no health expert myself but i  will tell you this that you should eat  properly and try to sleep  properly at least  i mean even if you're having nothing  special food no new i mean we all know  what hostel food is  but try to  eat regular hours okay that will i mean  automatically take care of a lot of  things if you eat regularly even if  nothing great food you're eating  and i know that engineering students and  science students they will invariably  sleep at unearthly hours  me advising you against that is not  going to change anything you will end up  doing those things  but still if possible  whatever weird hours you sleep try to be  regular even in that so your body will  have a certain  mechanism  in which it is comfortable so with these  pieces of advice i'll end this video i  wish you the very very best of luck so  all the best and i hope you have an  absolutely wonderful career ahead of you  thank you
 

